# Personal dotfiles

Shared Bash/Zsh, Git and command-line preferences. This is a base workstation
setup, not a machine image or an unattended server bootstrap.

Forgejo is the authoritative remote. GitHub is an optional outgoing mirror,
configured in Forgejo, not an independent source of changes.

## New Mac

Install Apple's command-line tools and, optionally, Homebrew from its official
site. Clone this repository; then run:

```sh
git clone git@forgejo.lab.kevinlebrun.io:kevinlebrun/dotfiles.git ~/dotfiles
cd ~/dotfiles
bash install.sh --dry-run
bash install.sh --with-packages
```

If Homebrew/tools are already handled separately, use `bash install.sh` alone.
The optional Brewfile installs Git, Neovim, ripgrep, jq, tree, tmux and wget.
`--no-upgrade` avoids upgrading existing packages; versions are not pinned.
No service is started. The installer never pulls/rebases the checkout, uses sudo,
changes macOS defaults, installs downloaded scripts or runs the legacy `.osx`.
Existing files and symlinks are moved into a unique, private backup directory
under `~/.local/state/dotfiles/backups/`. Repeating setup retains local overrides.
An alternate clone location is supported through a stable `~/dotfiles` symlink;
a different existing checkout is not overwritten.

## Configuration ownership

| Location | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `shell/env` | Portable PATH, editor and terminal environment |
| `shell/common` | Optional existing nvm and pyenv, with shell-specific initialization |
| `.zshrc`, `.bashrc` | Interactive preferences, aliases and prompt |
| `~/.shellrc_local` | Private machine overrides, sourced last; never replaced by setup |
| `~/.gitconfig_local` | Private machine identity, signing or merge tools; included last |

Setup creates comment-only local files with mode0600 when absent. It does not
copy the laptop's local files. No API token, vault access, SSH key, kubeconfig,
Talos configuration or OpenTofu state is needed for this base setup. Do not copy
secrets into versioned examples. Avoid automatically unlocking a vault or fetching
secrets at every shell startup. Configure 1Password/SSH/signing separately after
installation; the homelab repository has its own signing runbook.

The laptop's nvm/pyenv boilerplate now has a common equivalent. Its homelab aliases
and inference tokens remain machine/project-specific and are not auto-propagated.
Existing `.shellrc_local` may still duplicate old initialization: review it locally
without printing credentials. Do not delete that file wholesale.

## Deliberately separate

- Tailscale, oMLX/models, inference-service secrets and launchd configuration.
- macOS account/iCloud, Reminders permissions, SSH, FileVault, power/restart policy.
- Corporate SCFW, gitsign, Privileges, Trajectory and employer identity.
- Terminal-app settings, private SSH configuration and application preferences.
- Language-runtime installation; existing nvm/pyenv are optional, not provisioned.

The historic `.osx` script changes power, security and other system settings and
is not part of setup. Do not run it on a new Mac as a generic migration step.
The old Vim plugin configuration is opt-in with `--legacy-vim`; setup does not
fetch its plugins. Neovim starts with its own defaults unless configured separately.
`update-dependencies.sh` downloads unpinned helper scripts; it is not run by setup.

## Validation

```sh
bash -n install.sh .bashrc .bash_profile shell/env shell/common
zsh -n .zshrc .zprofile shell/env shell/common
bash install.sh --dry-run
```

A setup completion only proves file installation. Verify a new terminal, the
editor and Git identity on the target Mac. Base configuration does not prove
server boot availability or application access.

## Review notes — 2026-10-15

Removed hard-coded old work-account paths, corporate Bash wrappers and duplicate
LM Studio path blocks. Optional app directories now use the current home path.
Preserved the laptop's existing personal Git identity; local overrides can
replace it. Existing terminal and SSH app settings were inventoried only, not
exported wholesale. No whole-system defaults or local shell secret file is copied.

The old versioned shell/local.example contained literal credential-like values.
The current template is comment-only; history has not been rewritten and old
GitHub history remains. Their validity is unknown. Revoke/rotate any live keys
at the issuers before treating a public mirror as safe. Do not publish private
local overrides. No credential validity test, rotation or history rewrite was run.

The clone command assumes your existing Forgejo SSH access is configured. An
HTTPS clone through Forgejo is also possible with interactive authentication.
